---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";

// Reviewed and approved by the owner on 19 November 2026.
// Update when the email provider changes.
---
<Marketing
  title="Privacy | Pairpoll"
  description="What Pairpoll stores about creators and voters, who can see it, and when it is deleted. Polls, files and votes are deleted 30 days after a poll is created."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <PageIntro title="Privacy" lead="What Pairpoll stores, who can see it, and when it's deleted." />
    <div class="prose legal">
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated 19 November 2026</p>

      <h2>Who runs Pairpoll</h2>
      <p>Pairpoll is run by Vladimir Terekhov. Questions about your data: <a href="mailto:hello@pairpoll.com">hello@pairpoll.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>If you create polls</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address, so you can sign in with a one-time link. There is no password.</li>
        <li>Your polls: the question, the settings and the images or videos you upload.</li>
        <li>Sign-in links, sessions and API keys, stored only in a form that can't be turned back into the original.</li>
        <li>Counts used for limits, such as how many polls you created today and how much you uploaded.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If you vote</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The name you type, your picks and when you voted.</li>
        <li>A cookie that recognises your browser for that poll, so you can close the page and carry on later, and so each browser votes once.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You don't sign up to vote. Your name and your top list are visible to the person who made the poll. They can also
        choose to share the overall result with others, without voter names unless they decide to include them.
      </p>

      <h2>Reports</h2>
      <p>If you report a poll, we keep what you wrote so we can review it.</p>

      <h2>Abuse checks</h2>
      <p>
        Pairpoll uses Cloudflare Turnstile, an invisible check, when you sign in and when you start voting. Your IP address
        is used to limit abuse, for example how often sign-in links can be requested.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare Web Analytics counts page visits on every page without cookies. Google Analytics runs on our own pages
        only if you click Accept in the cookie pop-up, and never on voting pages. You can change your choice with "Cookie
        settings" at the bottom of the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Two kinds are needed for the service to work: a sign-in cookie for poll creators, and the voter cookie described
        above. Google Analytics cookies are added only if you accept them. There are no advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>When data is deleted</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every poll, with its files, votes and voter names, is deleted automatically 30 days after it was created.</li>
        <li>A poll's creator can delete a voter's entry, or the whole poll, at any time.</li>
        <li>You can delete your account, and all your polls with it, from your account settings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
      <p>
        Pairpoll runs on Cloudflare. Data is kept in Cloudflare's database and file storage. Sign-in emails are sent through
        Resend, an email delivery service.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>We don't sell your data and don't show ads.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Marketing>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-bottom: var(--s-8);
  }

  .legal-date {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
